# The Little Wins Telegram bot. Copy this file to bot/.env and fill it in:
#
#   cp bot/.env.example bot/.env && chmod 600 bot/.env
#
# bot/.env is git-ignored; never commit it. See "The Telegram bot" in docs/admin-guide.md.
# The bot is optional: the app doesn't need it. To turn it off, stop its container.

# From BotFather (/newbot). Required.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<token from BotFather>

# The one group the bot serves (a number, usually starting with -100). Leave it empty the first
# time: the bot then only logs the chats it is in ("Chat -100… (supergroup: …)"), so you can
# copy the ID here. It leaves any other group it is added to.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# From the Claude Console (API keys). Set a monthly spend limit there too. Required.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<key from the Claude Console>
# The model that answers. Default claude-haiku-5-5.
# BOT_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# The welcome check: minutes to tap the star (default 5) and wrong taps allowed (default 3).
# VERIFY_MINUTES=5
# VERIFY_TRIES=3

# Answers: at most this many per person per hour (default 10) and in all per day (default 300).
# Messages that don't look like questions or reports never reach Claude.
# ANSWERS_PER_USER_PER_HOUR=10
# ANSWERS_PER_DAY=300

# GitHub issues from bug reports and ideas, opened only when the person who wrote it taps the
# button. Optional: leave both empty to turn it off. The token: a fine-grained personal access
# token for this one repository with only "Issues: read and write".
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_REPO=nijaba/little-wins
# At most this many issues a day (default 5).
# ISSUES_PER_DAY=5
